WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.180
- Welcome back to our
post-game press conference.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.700
We've got the cast of 80 for Brady here,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.792
Jane Fonda, Lily Tomlin, Sally Field

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:11.643
and Rita Moreno everybody.

00:00:11.643 --> 00:00:13.830
Everybody played a great
interview today, I feel.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.480
Let's take some questions from the press.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.740
Let's start with Nick.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.120
Where are you Nick?

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:18.960
- Uh Kelly, right here.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.100
Thank you so much.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.630
Nick Krupke from FOX 12, Oregon.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.190
This question is for Jane.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:24.900
Earlier we saw Rita say

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.060
that she called you
for instructions in bed

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.220
and you had a curious look on your face?

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.050
Just wanted to know what
was going through your mind

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.190
at that moment?

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.573
- And do you have tips?

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:35.903
- Tits?

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:37.933
- Tips. (laughs)

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.676
- What'd she say?

00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:41.940
- Tits.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.230
- I did not say that HR.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.270
- I do not have ti... I have not

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.965
and I never will have tips for Rita.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:49.798
(crowd laughs)

00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:52.020
- [Kelly] Just not Rita. (laughs)

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.423
- Now Lily, on the other hand.

00:00:54.423 --> 00:00:55.980
(crowd laughs)

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.297
- You're just asking about
the wrong person. That's all.

00:01:00.297 --> 00:01:03.180
- All right. Where is
Mark? Mark, are you...

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.000
- Yeah. Right here. Mark
McClune, Arizona's family.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.710
Hey, so much was discussed today.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.040
I'm wondering that the proudest
moment in the discussion.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.660
And this question is for the whole panel

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.660
what you would've said and
done maybe differently.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.190
And we'll start with you, Lily.

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.970
- Oh my gosh. Well, that's
why I didn't join in

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.803
It was...

00:01:21.803 --> 00:01:24.120
(crowd laughs)

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.525
- Because you were ashamed?

00:01:25.525 --> 00:01:27.420
- If I was like really deeply honest.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.200
It was hard to compete with the

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.173
absolute uninhibited exposure.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.510
But I've always looked
to them as influences

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.655
and I've hung on every
word that they've said.

00:01:42.655 --> 00:01:45.238
(crowd laughs)

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.230
- Alright, let's go to Mario.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.640
What's your question, Mario?

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.980
- Yeah. Mario Solis. NBC4 Los Angeles.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.540
This question is for Rita.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.760
You came out of the gate strong.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.700
Dancing out of the helmet.
As a veteran in this game,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.860
Do you think it sort of set the stage

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.160
for the rest of the players?

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.290
- Oh, that wasn't my intention.
I heard music. I moved.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:07.740
(crowd laughs)

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.663
- That's what I do when I hear music.

00:02:11.469 --> 00:02:13.710
- Look at Sally! (laughs)

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.000
- [Mario] Kelly, now I have a follow up.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.833
- Okay. Follow up.

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:18.150
- So the follow-up
would be any of you wish

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.430
that you had also danced out like Rita?

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.263
- Oh God

00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:22.250
- No.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.280
(crowd laughs)

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.150
I do not.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.390
- No. We all go out of
our way to give Rita...

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.910
- We have to give Rita her space.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.960
- That's right. Yes.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.160
- Her hips don't lie.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.820
- I was trying very hard
behind her to dance.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.830
I guess it didn't register.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.620
- I have a question for one of you.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.680
Whoever wants to answer
this, I have a problem.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.150
And it came up a little bit

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.075
during the game now about tight ends.

00:02:49.075 --> 00:02:51.780
(crowd laughs)

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.703
I don't know what it means.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.710
Could you explain?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:00.020
I want one, but I don't
know quite what it is. So...

00:03:02.472 --> 00:03:03.510
- She appears to have found one.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.660
- [Kelly] Its so tight.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.110
What is a tight end?

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.346
That's a real question.

00:03:08.346 --> 00:03:09.630
- A position on a football team.

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.280
It's a position on a football team.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.213
It's a, it's a person that
plays the tight end position.

00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:16.080
Its not on the body.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.720
- But wait, but wait, they're
not the wide receiver.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.019
- Why is it called tight end?

00:03:21.019 --> 00:03:21.852
- Because he's...

00:03:21.852 --> 00:03:25.080
because he's tighter in, he's closer.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.480
- He's closer and always tighter in, okay.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.010
- He's closer, right?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.630
He's closer in.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:31.680
- A little closer to the quarterback.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.380
He's the receiver, runs the slot.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.800
- Is there sort of like a little short

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.080
with only like two or three guys in there

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.251
and they've all got
tight ends and they're...

00:03:43.251 --> 00:03:44.949
(crowd laughs)

00:03:44.949 --> 00:03:46.140
up and bounce one another? I don't...

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.720
- And what do you do to get a tight end?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.606
- Your workout videos.

00:03:49.606 --> 00:03:50.439
- You play football.

00:03:50.439 --> 00:03:51.480
- A lot of squats.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.720
- Exactly. You do some
Jane Fonda working out.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:55.670
That's what you do.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.852
That's how I got my tight end.

00:03:58.852 --> 00:04:00.510
All right. That is our show.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.449
A big thank you to the
cast of 80 for Brady!

00:04:03.449 --> 00:04:06.985
Jane Fonda, Lily Tomlin,
Sally Field ,Rita Moreno

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:09.914
and all the sports fans in our audience.

00:04:09.914 --> 00:04:11.880
And thank you as well
to a Stephen A. Smith.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.160
You love the Cowboys. I feel it.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.510
His book, Straight Shooter,

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.360
a memoir of second chances and first takes

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.830
is in stores now, go pick it up y'all.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.740
Have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

